# SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
sgi-replay 2
head sgi-mgras-ssi
# A deep double-buffered GL window on the SSI board, cut from a session
# trace of the clock program (a 100 by 100 window at screen (32, 32), display
# ID 17) running under the stock IRIX 6.5.30 X server and the IP27GR532
# libGLcore.so on a two-RE board. The program sends its draw-buffer
# command once, as (4, 1, 0): BACK of a deep visual is bit 2, never bit 1.
# Kept: every write the trace holds from its start
# up to the end of the second swap; dropped: reads, which a replay
# started mid-session cannot match. Added, because the trace begins after
# the X server programmed them: the two VC3 lines below, display enable and
# the base of the display-ID frame table, whose run lists the trace does
# carry.
#
# The kernel moves the bank token and the select bit together: token 0 and
# bit set (0x20000 under XMAP index 0, display ID 17) at the first swap,
# token 1 and bit clear at the second. Frame A is drawn while the token is
# 1, frame B while it is 0. Established by the trace: that sequence, and
# that the client names one back buffer. Inferred: that frame A sits in
# slot 2 and frame B in bank 0, so that the set bit shows slot 2 and the
# clear bit bank 0. Before the first swap the window shows bank 0, which
# nothing has drawn; after each swap the grey 0x333333 clear and a clock
# tick (0xe5e5e5) must show, and a model that scans out banks 0 and 1 only
# shows black after the first.
write 4 0x72038 0x1e000400
write 4 0x72038 0x4050000
